<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miles Macdonell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1767–1828</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miles Macdonell was a Scottish-born soldier and colonial administrator who served as the first governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a> from 1812. His Pemmican Proclamation of 1814, banning the export of pemmican from the colony's lands, angered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> and helped start the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemmican-war">Pemmican War</a>. He surrendered to the Nor'Westers in 1815 and was taken east under arrest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miles-macdonell.jpg" alt="Miles Macdonell" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manitoba Historical Society · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miles_MacDonell.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
